# Dependencies and build output
node_modules/
dist/
.venv-mlx/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Regenerable research artefacts. These are large (~23 GB together) and every
# one of them is reproducible from a documented command in REPRODUCE.md:
#   *.npy   exact distance tables from exact.py  (191 MB at k=6 alone)
#   *.npz   network + optimiser checkpoints from davi.py
# The JSON in eval/results/ is what the paper actually reads, and that IS tracked.
mlx-solver/*.npy
mlx-solver/*.npz

# Run logs. Local paths and timings only; nothing the paper depends on.
mlx-solver/*.log
mlx-solver/log_*.txt
mlx-solver/*.pid

# LaTeX intermediates
paper/*.aux
paper/*.bbl
paper/*.blg
paper/*.out
paper/*.log

.DS_Store

# Camera frames from the detector eval. These are photographs of a person and a
# home interior: the .jpg are obvious, but the .bin are the same images as raw
# 640x360x3 RGB and reconstruct in three lines of numpy, so excluding only the
# JPEGs would be pointless. Nothing in the paper depends on them. Capture your
# own with capture.html (see eval/README.md) to run the detector eval.
eval/frames/
paper/supplementary-anonymous.zip
